WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.504
This video shows how to put a band of
uncertainty

00:00:03.504 --> 00:00:07.770
around the simulated flow with SUFI-2 or
GLUE, and how to read the band.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.323
The Calibration page calls one run of the
model

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:14.310
with one set of parameter values a
simulation.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:18.000
One simulation gives one simulated flow
for each day.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.265
An uncertainty analysis makes many
simulations,

00:00:21.265 --> 00:00:26.480
each with another set of parameter values,
and keeps the simulated flow of each.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.876
The band is the range, on each day,

00:00:28.876 --> 00:00:32.390
between a low and a high value of these
simulated flows.

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:34.458
This video uses the model,

00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:39.341
the measured flow file and the three periods
of the video Calibrate and validate.

00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:44.945
In Set-up, click Clear choice and tick the
model 01020003,

00:00:44.945 --> 00:00:48.112
so that it is the only model chosen.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.551
Click Calibration, the fourth of the four
views.

00:00:52.751 --> 00:00:54.521
The box Model names the model.

00:00:55.022 --> 00:00:57.142
In the bar Method, click SUFI-2.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.010
SUFI-2 works in iterations.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:06.257
An iteration draws its sets of parameter
values by Latin hypercube sampling:

00:01:06.257 --> 00:01:11.770
the range of each parameter is cut into equal
parts, and each part gives one value.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:16.009
The band of the iteration is formed, on
each day,

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:19.390
by the 2.5 % and the 97.5 % values of the

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.100
simulated flows of the sets of the
iteration.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.550
Every simulation has the same weight.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:26.507
When it can,

00:01:26.507 --> 00:01:31.240
the iteration proposes new ranges of the
parameters for the next iteration.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.908
Under Measured data, check that the box
Measured file holds the path of

00:01:35.908 --> 00:01:38.784
the measured flow file of Calibrate and
validate,

00:01:38.784 --> 00:01:41.720
and that the line under it counts the
file's days.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.130
If the box is empty, click Download, as
the video Calibrate and validate shows.

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:58.723
Under Objective function, leave KGE daily.

00:01:59.223 --> 00:02:02.123
Under Years, type the years of the three
periods.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:20.439
In Simulations per iteration, type 50 and
press Enter.

00:02:21.944 --> 00:02:23.554
Click Start iteration 1.

00:02:24.662 --> 00:02:27.735
Under the boxes, a table lists three
steps:

00:02:27.735 --> 00:02:31.522
Initial simulation, Iteration 1 and Band,
new ranges.

00:02:31.722 --> 00:02:34.032
The block Result counts the simulations.

00:03:25.533 --> 00:03:29.433
The simulations take a while, and the
video goes on when they have ended.

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:34.519
The block Result now reads done.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.925
The chart Daily flow draws four things:

00:03:37.925 --> 00:03:42.992
the measured flow, the band named 95PPU,
the middle line named 50 %,

00:03:42.992 --> 00:03:46.420
and the simulated flow of the best
simulation.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.050
The shaded years are the calibration
years.

00:03:49.552 --> 00:03:54.182
The block Result gives the table 95PPU,
the table of the band.

00:03:54.684 --> 00:03:57.879
The p-factor is the share of the days with
a measured

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:01.074
flow on which the measured flow lies
inside the band.

00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:04.304
The r-factor is the mean width of the
band,

00:04:04.304 --> 00:04:07.795
divided by the standard deviation of the
measured flow.

00:04:08.295 --> 00:04:13.015
A p-factor near 1 means that the band
holds nearly all of the measured flows.

00:04:13.215 --> 00:04:18.085
A small r-factor means a narrow band compared
with the spread of the measured flow.

00:04:18.285 --> 00:04:23.094
A wider band holds at least as many
measured flows and has a larger r-factor,

00:04:23.094 --> 00:04:25.405
so the two factors are read together.

00:04:25.906 --> 00:04:30.986
The tab New ranges gives the range that
the iteration suggests for each parameter.

00:04:31.186 --> 00:04:34.296
A new range can be wider than the range
that was sampled.

00:04:34.496 --> 00:04:37.396
An iteration does not always narrow a
range.

00:04:40.535 --> 00:04:44.237
The band is made only from the simulations
that were made:

00:04:44.237 --> 00:04:47.875
parameter values drawn inside the ranges
set on the page.

00:04:48.075 --> 00:04:51.675
No error of the measured flow or of the
weather is added to it.
